# Binary-master probe re-run under a newer solver stack (SciPy 1.16.3 / HiGHS as shipped),
# Python 3.13.9, executed 2026-10-11 on the author's Apple-Silicon machine.
# The archived results/cap_expansion_milp.{json,txt} were produced with SciPy 1.15.3
# (Python 3.10), the environment documented in the paper. Every entry agrees across the
# two versions except the diffuse (vol=0) est-det cell, where the near-degenerate
# stale-cut tie-breaking resolves differently: in the archived run one of the two seeds
# fails to certify within the 200-iteration cap (5,975 evaluations) while in this re-run
# both seeds certify at iteration 150 (4,525 evaluations each).
# The cell is deterministic within this environment: a repeat run of est-det vol=0
# returns 4,525 / iteration 150 / certified for both seeds again, bit for bit.
# The documented SciPy 1.15.3 environment cannot be reconstituted on this machine:
# its compiled extensions fail to load (dlopen fails on many .so files),
# so the archived numbers are the record of the 1.15.3 stack and this file is the
# record of the 1.16.3 stack, with the one differing cell stated above.
#
